.next/
node_modules/

# Draft worktrees. A draft checkout lives at `.worktrees/draft_<id>` inside the
# app tree, so without this the deploy upload walks a full copy of the site per
# open draft. Two failures follow: the upload blows Vercel's file-count cap on
# an app with several drafts, and `draft_service` creates and removes these
# directories while the CLI is enumerating, so a path vanishes mid-walk and the
# upload dies on ENOENT. Nothing under here ships.
.worktrees/
.git/

# Secrets. The secret vault writes runtime env into `.env` in the app tree, so
# without this the raw file ships with the deploy upload. Safe to exclude: the
# deployed app does not read it — `vercel_deploy_service._sync_environment_variables`
# reads the vault and pushes every key to Vercel as a PROJECT env var, which is
# what the running site actually resolves.
#
# Note this does NOT stop a vault secret reaching production: that sync is
# unconditional. Keeping a write-capable credential (a CMS management token)
# out of production needs an exclusion in that sync, or storing it outside the
# vault entirely.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
